WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.849 --> 00:00:05.270
From day one, Shemar Moore's Derek Morgan
was the charm and muscle at the heart of Criminal

00:00:05.270 --> 00:00:06.270
Minds.

00:00:06.270 --> 00:00:10.650
He made it through 11 seasons barely that
included wrestling with bad guys and childhood

00:00:10.650 --> 00:00:14.070
demons, not to mention being framed, kidnapped,
and tortured.

00:00:14.070 --> 00:00:18.090
Finally, enough was enough for both the character
and the actor who played him.

00:00:18.090 --> 00:00:23.410
Moore officially departed from the long-running
crime drama on March 23, 2016 in an episode

00:00:23.410 --> 00:00:28.340
that saw his character's fiancée survive
a gunshot wound and give birth to their child.

00:00:28.340 --> 00:00:32.500
And that was just two episodes after Morgan's
own near death experience.

00:00:32.500 --> 00:00:37.010
Suffice to say that having a baby changed
Morgan's perspective on his career, and he

00:00:37.010 --> 00:00:40.829
decided to step away from the action-packed
life and his colleagues in the Behavioral

00:00:40.829 --> 00:00:42.519
Analysis Unit.

00:00:42.519 --> 00:00:46.610
Since then, Moore has returned to both CBS
and the role of crime-fighting action hero

00:00:46.610 --> 00:00:49.639
with a troubled past, playing Hondo on S.W.A.T.

00:00:49.639 --> 00:00:53.969
But despite his talent for playing tough guys
who won't say no to a fight, in real life,

00:00:53.969 --> 00:00:58.179
Moore's reasons for bidding farewell to his
most famous role are surprisingly similar

00:00:58.179 --> 00:01:00.969
to Morgan's reasons for leaving the BAU.

00:01:00.969 --> 00:01:05.409
It took eight years for flirtatious workaholic
Morgan to find a steady girlfriend.

00:01:05.409 --> 00:01:06.740
As Moore put it to TV Guide,

00:01:06.740 --> 00:01:12.280
"You never saw [Morgan's] off-the-clock side,
where he lets his hair down, dates, has drinks

00:01:12.280 --> 00:01:14.060
and has somebody in his life."

00:01:14.060 --> 00:01:18.780
In the first episode of season 9, the character
finally mentioned a girlfriend but it took

00:01:18.780 --> 00:01:23.920
another eight episodes to meet the lucky lady
who would become his fiancée, Savannah, a

00:01:23.920 --> 00:01:26.380
doctor at Bethesda General Hospital.

00:01:26.380 --> 00:01:29.130
Moore can relate to his character's overdue
love life.

00:01:29.130 --> 00:01:32.320
In fact, that's one reason he gave for stepping
away from the role.

00:01:32.320 --> 00:01:36.780
A few months after his last episode aired,
he told TV Guide that he said goodbye to Criminal

00:01:36.780 --> 00:01:37.780
Minds,

00:01:37.780 --> 00:01:39.549
"... so I could pursue other avenues of my
life.

00:01:39.549 --> 00:01:42.950
I want to get married, I want to have kids,
I want to travel."

00:01:42.950 --> 00:01:47.760
A few years on, and it appears that unlike
Morgan, Moore has yet to find the person he

00:01:47.760 --> 00:01:49.170
wants to settle down with.

00:01:49.170 --> 00:01:53.469
He's been romantically linked to several famous
women since leaving Criminal Minds, including

00:01:53.469 --> 00:01:59.450
soccer player Shawna Gordon, whom he dated
from 2014 to 2015, and actress Anabelle Acosta.

00:01:59.450 --> 00:02:04.060
In 2018, he told Steve Harvey that he and
Acosta were taking things slow, while also

00:02:04.060 --> 00:02:06.829
emphasizing that he was looking for a long-term
partner, saying,

00:02:06.829 --> 00:02:11.500
"I've done everything I could do by myself,
and now I need that somebody I need that partner

00:02:11.500 --> 00:02:14.270
in crime to do the rest of what I want to
do."

00:02:14.270 --> 00:02:19.580
Unfortunately, Acosta was not that partner:
the pair split in 2019, and Moore's mission

00:02:19.580 --> 00:02:21.660
to find love continues.

00:02:21.660 --> 00:02:26.030
The other reason Moore gave for leaving Criminal
Minds was both personal and professional.

00:02:26.030 --> 00:02:28.020
In that same TV Guide chat, he revealed,

00:02:28.020 --> 00:02:31.880
"I'm just ready to grow [...] I'm not leaving
to go make a bunch of money [...] I'm leaving

00:02:31.880 --> 00:02:36.530
because I just creatively want to be fueled,
and [I'm] excited to try new things and see

00:02:36.530 --> 00:02:38.370
what else I'm capable of."

00:02:38.370 --> 00:02:43.460
After departing from Criminal Minds, Moore
starred in the 2016 rom-com The Bounce Back,

00:02:43.460 --> 00:02:45.150
which he also executive produced.

00:02:45.150 --> 00:02:48.960
The film looked like it might be Moore's chance
to break the mold, as he went from portraying

00:02:48.960 --> 00:02:54.400
an FBI Special Agent to playing an unlucky-in-love,
self-styled "relationship expert."

00:02:54.400 --> 00:02:58.500
The Bounce Back received respectable reviews
from critics and audiences, but it ultimately

00:02:58.500 --> 00:03:01.910
flew under the radar, and didn't make much
of an impact for Moore.

00:03:01.910 --> 00:03:06.730
The actor also continued lending his voice
to the character of Victor Stone (a.k.a. Cyborg)

00:03:06.730 --> 00:03:11.450
across several animated DC projects, which
he had done even when he was still working

00:03:11.450 --> 00:03:12.450
on Criminal Minds.

00:03:12.450 --> 00:03:15.160
"Good work, team!

00:03:15.160 --> 00:03:18.000
Too bad Shazam and Lantern had to miss the
fun."

00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:23.680
In 2017, Moore went back to television for
S.W.A.T., a remake of ABC's short-lived '70s

00:03:23.680 --> 00:03:27.700
cop series that is still going strong as of
the making of this video.

00:03:27.700 --> 00:03:33.070
Moore told CBS This Morning in October 2017
that his role on S.W.A.T. is his "dream job."

00:03:33.070 --> 00:03:36.630
"This is my dream job because I've always
believed what I'm capable of.

00:03:36.630 --> 00:03:40.530
I get to be a lead, which I'm proud of, but
I'm also smart enough and humble enough to

00:03:40.530 --> 00:03:42.640
know that I can't do it by myself."

00:03:42.640 --> 00:03:46.820
It was certainly sad to see Moore leave Criminal
Minds, but fans can take heart knowing that

00:03:46.820 --> 00:03:51.080
he's happy where he is now, and will likely
be a prime-time mainstay for years to come.

